WEBVTT

00:00:00.678 --> 00:00:05.011
Tutorial two. Variables, refraction and visual acuity.

00:00:09.405 --> 00:00:17.871
Files often mix plus and minus cylinder. List each sphere, cylinder and axis set, and the plus-cylinder rows are converted for you.

00:00:18.154 --> 00:00:26.574
Next, say which notation your visual acuity uses: decimal, logMAR, Snellen, or ETDRS letters.

00:00:26.802 --> 00:00:33.318
The statistics can run in logMAR. The figures and the export tabs receive the right scale automatically.

00:00:33.538 --> 00:00:41.958
Give each variable a section and a statistical type. The type decides the summary and the test, and each test is named in the output.

00:00:42.176 --> 00:00:46.928
Set the row order of your tables, so they read like the table in your manuscript.

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:57.230
Variables recorded once per person, such as age and sex, are listed here. They are counted per patient, not per eye.

00:00:58.029 --> 00:01:02.502
StandardEyes. For ophthalmologists, by ophthalmologists.

